[10.188185, "o", "I created `calc/__init__.py` and `tests/test_calc.py`, then added the third argument. All four tests pass.\r\n\r\n- **`calc/__init__.py`**: `add(a, b, c=0)` returns `a + b + c`.\r\n- **`tests/test_calc.py`**: two tests for the original two-argument behavior (positive and negative numbers), plus two for the new argument: one checks `add(1, 2, 3) == 6`, and one checks that omitting `c` gives the same result as passing `0`.\r\n\r\nI ran `python3 -m pytest -q tests/test_calc.py` from `/work`; `python` isn't on the PATH here, so I used `python3`. The `calc` import works because the test is run from `/work`.\r\n"]
